Topic : Difference between Kill ,kill -9 ,Kill -3 

1.kill 1234    # Graceful shutdown (SIGTERM)
2.kill -3 1234   # Request thread dump (for JVM)
3.kill -9 1234   # Force kill (no questions asked)

>kill or kill -15 (SIGTERM)
Default signal when you run kill.
Gives the process a chance to clean up.
Best for graceful shutdowns.

 >kill -3 (SIGQUIT)
Used to generate thread dumps in Java apps.
JVM writes thread info to stdout/stderr or log files.
Doesn’t kill the process (unless specifically programmed to do so).

>kill -9 (SIGKILL)
Immediately terminates the process.
No cleanup, no saving state — just dies.
Useful when a process is unresponsive.
Should be used as a last resort.
